The Gilded Spire is the seat of [[Org/Omnivox/index|Omnivox]], standing in orbit over [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] in what was once Station 7, a television station that went dark and was built over. The whole station is the company's, and its main draw is a casino that admits the very wealthy. To enter it is to enter another country: a visitor passes through customs and a check-in like a hotel's.

The station is a slab of metal a mile long with rings of gold floating about its middle for show. Ships pass through a barrier at its underside that keeps the air and heat in, and dock along the first floor's space pier. From the pier, stairs climb under a wide archway into the station, and cargo hallways branch off to either side.

Floor 2 is the lobby, floored in black stone and plates of real gold beneath gold pillars and filigree over titanium. The employees there have skin of gold, not painted but replaced. Guests queue at check-in desks along one side, and a plainer hall on the other leads to a bank of elevators, which carry no buttons and take a rider to whichever floor was set before they entered. Floors 3 to 112 are offices, and floor 113 is a garden planted with flora from another world, set between the working floors and the executives above. Floors 114 to 125 hold the executive offices, the directory skips floor 126, and the penthouse is 127. A back stair on the office floors climbs as far as floor 113 and stops, short of the executives.

In the Rhett, the dream laid over Syrin, the garden is shattered, a pane broken into overlapping pieces, and [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)/Gilded Spire/Wriggling Man|the Wriggling Man]] waits there.
